{"version":2,"width":100,"height":28,"env":{"SHELL":"bash","TERM":"xterm-256color"},"title":"QA-Z terminal demo: do_not_merge to verified repair"}
[0.2,"o","$ pipx install git+https://github.com/qazedhq/qa-z.git\r\n"]
[0.8,"o","installed package qa-z from GitHub alpha source\r\n"]
[1.1,"o","$ qa-z demo auth-bug\r\n"]
[1.7,"o","created isolated demo: .qa-z/demo/auth-bug\r\nbaseline: risky auth change captured\r\ncandidate: fixed implementation included for verification\r\n"]
[2.0,"o","$ cd .qa-z/demo/auth-bug\r\n"]
[2.3,"o","$ qa-z guard --from-run latest --adapter codex\r\n"]
[3.1,"o","QA-Z Guard\r\nVerdict: do_not_merge\r\nReason: auth/owner-check risk detected\r\nNext: qa-z repair-prompt --from-run latest --adapter codex\r\n"]
[3.4,"o","$ qa-z repair-prompt --from-run latest --adapter codex\r\n"]
[4.1,"o","repair prompt: .qa-z/runs/latest/repair/codex.md\r\nrepair evidence: tests failed before merge, deep auth rule flagged risk\r\n"]
[4.5,"o","$ qa-z verify --baseline-run .qa-z/runs/baseline --candidate-run .qa-z/runs/candidate\r\n"]
[5.2,"o","verify verdict: improved\r\nresolved: py_test, sg_scan\r\nblocking_before: 2\r\nblocking_after: 0\r\n"]
